WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.960
Rock, paper, scissors is an ancient
game of cunning and chance.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.760
If only there was a way to improve
those chances.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.000
Turns out there are a few
key strategies.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.960
The game is mainly about predicting
and reading your opponent.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.400
So what if you could predict
their first hand?

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.120
Research has shown
that there is a slight preference

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.800
for people to begin by playing rock.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.160
There are different theories
about why -

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.200
it could be because

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.440
it is mentioned first

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.640
in the name of the game,

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.600
or it could be because

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.080
rock is similar to a fist

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.600
which seems powerful.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.560
So if we know that, it gives us
an edge - just play paper.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.560
Research shows that people who lose
a hand tend to change.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.360
So there is a reasonable chance
that our opponent

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.480
will change to scissors or paper.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.160
That gives us our second edge -

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.160
just play scissors and we should
either win or draw.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.760
But this isn't an exact science.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.160
What if it doesn’t go to plan
and your opponent wins?

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.520
Perhaps they know
a bit of game strategy too.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.480
If we lost the previous hand

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.320
then our opponent might
reasonably expect us to switch

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.480
to something else.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.720
This gives us our final edge -

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.080
surprise them by sticking
with our previous choice.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.760
Hopefully they'll switch,

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.680
expecting us to switch,
and it should improve our chances.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.080
The less predictable you are, the
better chance you have of winning.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.660
Thanks for watching! :)

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:06.920
